{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791470801,"nonce":"QsCZ6wXVqMMqQo3WMWjCyRoAvpQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABV42JbQ","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/159","origin":"github"},"title":"FieldView FD partials crash under JIT: int(jnp.sqrt(...)) raises ConcretizationTypeError","message":"## Summary\n\n`FieldView` FD partial derivatives (`.x`, `.y`, `.xx`, `.yy`, `.xy`, …) on a 2-D structured mesh crash during JIT compilation with a `ConcretizationTypeError`.\n\n## Bug\n\nIn `jno/differential_operators.py`, the number of variables is computed as\n\n```python\nn_vars = int(jnp.sqrt(len(var_dims)))\n```\n\nat three sites (lines ~206, ~624, ~1044). Under JIT, `jnp.sqrt` returns a JAX tracer, and calling `int()` on a tracer raises:\n\n```\njax.errors.ConcretizationTypeError: Abstract tracer value encountered where concrete value is required.\n```\n\nThis makes **every** `.xx` / `.yy` / `.xy` derivative on a 2-D structured mesh fail at compile time, i.e. the documented pattern\n\n```python\nu = NN(a_phys).field.bind(x=x, y=y)\nresidual = u.xx + u.yy + f\n```\n\ndoes not run at all.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the JAX call with a pure-Python square root:\n\n```python\nn_vars = int(len(var_dims) ** 0.5)\n```\n\nThe 3-D analog in the same file already uses the pure-Python form, so this was the odd one out.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\nimport jno\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nd = jno.shape.rect(0, 0, 1, 1, size=0.05).domain(compute_mesh_connectivity=True)\nx, y = d.variable(\"interior\")\nu = jnp.sin(jnp.pi * x) * jnp.sin(jnp.pi * y)   # or any mesh-shaped field\nu.field.bind(x=x, y=y).xx                       # -\u003e ConcretizationTypeError under JIT\n```\n\n## Environment\n\n- jNO (current `main`)\n- JAX (CPU), JIT enabled","files":null}]}